==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|caterwrawe|lang=enm}} (one of numerous earlier variants); from {{term|cater||cat|lang=enm}} + {{term|wrawen|lang=enm}}/{{term|wrawlen||cry like a cat|lang=enm}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{hyphenation|ca|ter|waul|lang=en}}
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/ˈkæt.ə.wɔːl/|lang=en}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈkæt.ɚ.wɔl/|/ˈkæt.ɚ.wɑl/|lang=en}}
* {{a|cot-caught|northern cities vowel shift}} {{IPA|/ˈkæt.ɚ.wɑl/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-caterwaul.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{context|intransitive|lang=en}} To [[cry]] as cats [[in heat]]; to make a [[harsh]], [[offensive]] [[noise]].
# {{context|intransitive|lang=en}} To have a [[noisy]] [[argument]], like cats.

